messages.content:
The test
['org.apache.commons.codec.binary.Base32Test.testCodec200()']
failed.

The test looks like: 
    @Test
    public void testCodec200() {
        final Base32 codec = new Base32(true, (byte)'W'); // should be allowed
        assertNotNull(codec);
    }

Current bug report: 
{
    "summary": "Base32.HEX_DECODE_TABLE contains the wrong value 32"
    "description": "At line 99:\n 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, // 50-57 O-V\nthe value 32 should not be included. That disallows to use 'W' as padding with hex table.\n"
}

Recent bug reports: 
RPT#CODEC-199: {
 "summary": "Bug in HW rule in Soundex"
 "description": "The Soundex algorithm says that if two characters that map to the same code are separated by H or W, the second one is not encoded. However, in the implementation (in Soundex.getMappingCode() line 191), a character that is preceded by two characters that are either H or W, is not encoded, regardless of what the last consonant was. Source: <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soundex#American_Soundex>"
}
